# Module Workspace UI Contract

Purpose: keep clinical and operational module screens visually and behaviorally consistent.

**Scope:** applies to **new** screens and **material** changes to existing workspace pages. Legacy large pages may be refactored incrementally; do not block urgent fixes on full extraction.

## Mandatory layout stack

Module work queues (OPD, IPD, Lab, Billing, Nursing, etc.) must use this stack unless the interaction model is fundamentally different (e.g. auth, simple settings):

| Layer | Shared widget | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| Page root | `AsyncStateScaffold` | loading, error, retry ([`ui-feedback.mdc`](./ui-feedback.mdc)) |
| Page width | `ResponsivePage` + `PageMaxWidth` | padding and max width ([`layouts.mdc`](./layouts.mdc)) |
| Workspace shell | `AppWorkspace` | title, worklist, detail, status tone; queue counts via toolbar notifications submenu |
| Worklist | `AppListTable` | columns, pagination, mobile list fallback, selection |
| Detail | `AppWorkspaceDetailPanel` | selected item sections |
| Actions | `AppActionPanel` / `AppActionList` | primary actions grouped by role/state |
| Mutations | `AppDialog`, `AppWorkspaceMutationDialog` | focused forms; not full-page for small edits |

Import from `package:hosspi_hms/shared/layout/layout.dart`, `shared/components/components.dart`, and `shared/actions/actions.dart` before adding feature-local equivalents.

## Mandatory behavior (aligned with OPD/IPD flows)

- **Notifications submenu (More actions) filters** the current worklist — it must not open modal lists of the same data.
- **Hide zero-value notification rows** when the workspace pattern expects it.
- **Hospital workflow language** in labels — never expose raw enum names, API stage codes, or internal IDs to users.
- **Entity references** — surface `human_friendly_id` (and patient display name where applicable). Backend maps internal IDs; never show raw table IDs or UUIDs in production UI, URLs, or client-held identifiers.
- **Role + state + subscription gating** — show actions only when backend stage, user permission, and subscription entitlement all allow; disable with tooltip when helpful.
- **Performance and simplicity** — keep worklists paginated/lazy; minimize steps for common queue actions; preserve uniform spacing, tokens, and component usage across modules.
- **Responsiveness** — workspace shell must adapt across mobile, tablet, and desktop per [`layouts.mdc`](./layouts.mdc).
- **Row refresh** — after small modal mutations, refresh the affected row, detail panel, summary counts, and nav badges; avoid full-page reload when the controller supports targeted refresh.
- **Realtime** — subscribe to the module's `RealtimeEventGroups` where the feature already defines one.

## Forbidden patterns

- Custom full-page `Scaffold` + hand-rolled table for a module that fits the workspace contract.
- Duplicate status chips (one clearance state is enough; do not stack redundant badges).
- Private feature string classes (`_BillingText`, `_IcuText`, etc.) — use `app_en.arb` ([`localization_i18n.mdc`](./localization_i18n.mdc)).
- Hard-coded colors, spacing, or `TextStyle` in feature presentation code ([`design-system.mdc`](./design-system.mdc)).
- Inline `SnackBar` success copy that bypasses localization.
- Creating a new table/list component when `AppListTable` satisfies the need.

## File organization

| File | Max guidance | Owns |
|---|---|---|
| `*_workspace_page.dart` | prefer `< 800` lines | composition, wiring |
| `presentation/widgets/` | extract when page grows | notification builders, detail sections, dialogs |
| `*_workspace_controller.dart` | — | mutations, filters, selection |

When a workspace page exceeds ~800 lines, extract widgets before adding more inline UI.

## Reusability

- All components suitable for reuse across modules **must** be implemented as reusable components and stored under `frontend/lib/shared/` — never duplicate workspace patterns in feature folders.
- Check the shared component catalog before creating new UI elements; one implementation per interaction pattern.

## Before adding UI (checklist)

1. Search `frontend/lib/shared/` for an existing component or pattern.
2. Open a reference module with the same shape (e.g. Lab, Billing, IPD) and match its structure.
3. Add `app_en.arb` keys before user-facing strings.
4. Confirm permissions via `AccessGate` / `AppAccessActionGate`.

